# Prisma: Migrations Only (No `db push`)

This project **does not** use `prisma db push` for schema changes. All schema changes are **versioned migration files** under `prisma/migrations/`.

## Do not run

- `prisma db push`
- `npm run db:push`
- `db push --force-reset` or any push-based sync for routine schema work

(`db:push:prod` / `push-prod-schema.js` are legacy — prefer `migrate deploy` unless the user explicitly requests the prod push script.)

## Standard workflow

1. Edit `prisma/schema.prisma`
2. Create and apply a migration locally:
   ```bash
   npx prisma migrate dev --name short_descriptive_name
   ```
3. Regenerate the client (also runs on `migrate dev`, but restart dev server if the client was cached):
   ```bash
   npm run db:generate
   ```
4. Commit the new folder under `prisma/migrations/` with the migration SQL

## Applying migrations

| Environment | Command |
|-------------|---------|
| Local (existing DB, pull latest migrations) | `npx prisma migrate deploy` |
| Local (creating a new migration while developing) | `npx prisma migrate dev --name ...` |
| Production / shared remote | `npx prisma migrate deploy` (after review; never `migrate reset`) |

## New machine / fresh local DB

After `DATABASE_URL` is set:

```bash
npm run db:generate
npx prisma migrate deploy
```

## Safety

- Migrations must be **additive** when possible (no drops/truncates without explicit user approval)
- See also: `no-database-deletion` rule — no `migrate reset` on production or shared data
- Full reference: `docs/database-migrations.md`
